Z||000000||Spektrum-87GT||09-11-2001||07:13 PM||||alright... i'll admit it... i take it to at least 4k for 1st, 2nd, and 3rd gear... how much damage am i doing to the engine/transaxle? i just cant help myself, i owned a cavalier and a jeep before this, finally have some pick-up! seriously though, if i keep this up am i going to shorten the life of the engine or transaxle majorly? i can deal with a little bit   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'm more worried about the transaxle because I plan on a 3.4 swap next summer.<P>sorry, forgot, its a 5 speed getrag, rebuilt 30k miles ago<P>------------------<BR>87 fiero gt under semi restoration/modification. progress at <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/spektrum_87gt/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/spektrum_87gt/</A><p>[This message has been edited by Spektrum-87GT (edited 09-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||09-11-2001||09:14 PM||||Only 4 grand? <P>On my Fiero (85 GT) my power curve feels like it starts at 3!<P>The engine makes its best horsepower at 4500 rpm and best torque at 3600 rpm and you are worried about over revving it????<P>Quit yer whining and have fun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Spektrum-87GT||09-11-2001||09:58 PM||||heh, will do! i guess i'm just used to my inline 6 4.0 jeep engine... it sounds like its about to blow up at 3k rpms, and i always switched at 2-2.5k, this is going to take some getting used to, but i like it!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Leadfoot||09-12-2001||12:21 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spektrum-87GT:<BR><B>heh, will do! i guess i'm just used to my inline 6 4.0 jeep engine... it sounds like its about to blow up at 3k rpms, and i always switched at 2-2.5k, this is going to take some getting used to, but i like it!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well I have a 4 banger jeep and at 3 grand it would scream like a banshee....that is until I put a complete borla system on it.  (this is where you say....on a 4 banger!?)  Well believe it or not the borla header and exhaust eliminated that problem.  I now take the engine to its limit and it still sounds like it can take more.  Anyway, back to your question, if the engine was recently built I would say you shouldn't worry too much.  However, if it had 130k on it I would say ease off.  At that kind of mileage you are asken for rebuild.  Trust me I speak from experience.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||artherd||09-12-2001||03:26 AM||||If you're not bouncing off redline (or a rev-limiter  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  you're not driving it right  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Hrm, I wonder why I have three fieros, and ALL have engine problems ?<P>POS 2.8, we have to ask if it's safe at 4grand. Heck, it dosen't even make power UNTILL 4kRPM!! :S)<P>(that said, beware of 2.8s with over 100k, you'll spin a bearing right quick.  The good news is, pick just about any engine and put it in, chances are it will be better than the 2.8i  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000005||88formula||09-12-2001||09:54 PM||||4k is nothing!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||2birds||09-12-2001||10:06 PM||||For the last 13+ years, 171,00 miles and counting, I've routinely run it up to 4500 rpm in regular driving.  I shift fairly hard, too.  Only thing I've worn out has been clutches at 60k, but the Getrag and 2.8 are relatively untouched.  I don't attempt burnouts, and I have been religious about oil and filter every 2000-2500 miles, Havoline 10W-40 and AC Delco filter.  Cold weather, it gets 5W-30.||||reg||1
